      },
      "note": [
        "For the period 1970–1986 there are no estimates for persons aged 20–24, this is indicated by “..” in the time series.  \r\nFor the period 1970–2000 the population was 16–64 years of age. For this reason there are no estimates for persons aged 15–74, 15–19, 15–24, 65–74, this is indicated by “..” in the time series.  \r\nFor the period 1970–2004 the time series contains “linked data”. No margins of error (uncertainty figures) for this period are present, this is indicated by “..” in the time series.",
        "As the LFS is a sample survey, all estimations are subject to uncertainty. Uncertainty in estimations based on fewer than 20 observations on a monthly or quarterly basis or fewer than 40 observations on a yearly basis may be considered too large and the estimation is not reported. In these cases, the value is replaced with two periods [..].",
        "As of 1 January 2021, the LFS is carried out in accordance with the new EU framework regulation. This means there is a break in time series between 2020 and 2021.  \r\n[The Statistical Database, data from 2021](https://www.statistikdatabasen.scb.se/pxweb/sv/ssd/START__AM__AM0401/)  \r\n[The Statistical Database, data up to and including 2020](https://www.statistikdatabasen.scb.se/pxweb/sv/ssd/START__AM__AM0403/)"
      ],
